{"id":22662875173154,"type":"album","name":"Sonic Prayer","artist":"Earthless","year":2005,"weight":16,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710903.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-ab4639dd-6ad2-446c-8582-f643c5c2e7db/mbid-ab4639dd-6ad2-446c-8582-f643c5c2e7db-13036032474.jpg","scaruffi":7.0,"yt":"vV87qhEJOUQ","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/7qsRoK0t5DcVoWHumbEqZ6","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_mj-77zEx9mYRdrZqeqt5GXm-olVvNROW0","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/earthless/sonic-prayer"},"desc":"It’s tough to write a review for a two song album without diving into the minutia of each track. And a minute-by-minute recap is about as interesting as instructions on how to make ice, even if the album is incredible. So the basic details of Earthless’ Sonic Prayer are thus: “Flower Travelin’ Man” is an extended acid rock jam with a drumbeat that’s similar to Zeppelin’s “Immigrant Song,” a bass line like Maiden’s “Wrathchild,” and guitar playing that channels Hendrix. It’s goes on and on, getting better and better. “Lost in the Cold Sun” takes on a more Middle Eastern ."},"artist_ref":{"id":148189707890659,"name":"Earthless","info":{"img":null}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":147423806094006,"type":"genre","name":"Psychedelic Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":690,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":109063683126539,"type":"genre","name":"Hard Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":562,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":55893123468232,"type":"genre","name":"Experimental Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":373,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":8601518715705,"type":"genre","name":"Stoner Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":239,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":77376330613218,"type":"genre","name":"Stoner Metal","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":213,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":274248615246800,"type":"genre","name":"instrumental rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":18,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":26